[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:26. The Best Art Critics]
[00:00.540]Passage 26 | 文章二十六
[00:02.735]The best art critics. | 最好的艺术评论家。
[00:05.955]I am an art student and I paint a lot of pictures. | 我是一名艺术系学生，我画了很多画。
[00:11.700]Many people pretend that they understand modern art. | 许多人假装他们懂现代艺术。
[00:16.490]They always tell you what a picture is about. | 他们总是告诉你一幅画是关于什么的。
[00:20.520]Of course, many pictures are not about anything. | 当然，许多画根本不是关于任何东西的。
[00:24.815]They are just pretty patterns. | 它们只是漂亮的图案。
[00:27.375]We like them in the same way that we like pretty curtain material. | 我们喜欢它们，就像我们喜欢漂亮的窗帘布一样。
[00:32.600]I think that young children often appreciate modern pictures better than anyone else. | 我认为小孩子往往比其他人更能欣赏现代画。
[00:39.660]They notice more. | 他们注意得更多。
[00:41.805]My sister is only seven, but she always tells me whether my pictures are good or not. | 我妹妹只有七岁，但她总是告诉我我的画好不好。
[00:49.450]She came into my room yesterday. | 昨天她走进我的房间。
[00:52.985]What are you doing? | 你在做什么？
[00:55.230]she asked. | 她问。
[00:56.790]I'm hanging this picture on the wall. | 我正把这幅画挂在墙上。
[00:59.570]I answered. | 我回答。
[01:00.815]It's a new one. | 这是新画的。
[01:02.440]Do you like it? | 你喜欢吗？
[01:04.530]She looked at it critically for a moment. | 她批判性地看了一会儿。
[01:08.265]It's all right, she said. | “还行，”她说。
[01:11.420]But isn't it upside down? | 但它是不是倒了？
[01:14.525]I looked at it again. | 我又看了一眼。
[01:16.920]She was right. | 她是对的。
[01:18.565]It was. | 确实是。